## Development principles
- Keep changes minimal and focused — match existing patterns in the repo
- Meaningful names; no mystery abbreviations
- Ask when requirements are ambiguous; do not guess and patch
- No secrets in code — use environment variables
- Comments only for non-obvious business logic

## Git & commits
- Commit style: {{ team.conventions.commit_style if team.get('conventions') else '[scope] short description' }}
- Small, logical commits; verify with diff before declaring done
- Prefer PRs under {{ team.conventions.pr_max_loc if team.get('conventions') else 400 }} LOC when possible

## Agent behaviour
- Plan before large features (use Plan mode or a short design note)
- Clear context when switching unrelated tasks
- Run tests and lint before marking work complete
- Visual QA in the browser for UI changes when applicable

